{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarpPedals\/color","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlharppedals\/color"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"title":"color","role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLHarpPedalsV5colorAA8MXLColorVSgvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"symbolKind":"property"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarpPedals"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","title":"MXLColor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLHarpPedals":{"type":"topic","title":"MXLHarpPedals","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLHarpPedals","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlharppedals","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarpPedals","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLHarpPedals","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The harp-pedals type is used to create harp pedal diagrams. The pedal-step and pedal-alter elements use the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same values as the step and alter elements. For easiest reading, the pedal-tuning elements should follow"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"standard harp pedal order, with pedal-step values of D, C, B, E, F, G, and A."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLHarpPedals/color":{"title":"color","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLHarpPedals\/color","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlharppedals\/color","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, v